<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bentley, Gerhardt & Bates (2008) PLoS Comput. Biol., Hellström et al. (2007) Nature & Jakobsson et al. (2010) Nat. Cell Biol. VEGF-VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 tip/stalk salt-and-pepper lateral inhibition and angiogenic sprouting, coupled to lumenized Poiseuille flow, wall-shear pruning and arteriovenous specification (Pass 3) — Code-to-model traceability: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-100) maps every governing equation of Sections 2-3b to its paper and to the five Lean theorems with file#line pins; the Section 3b banner (L519-535) states the reduced-model scope and residuals explicitly; `pries_shear_set_point_pa`, `solve_poiseuille_network`, `fit_murray_exponent` and `simulate_perfused_plexus_remodeling` cite Pries 1995/1998, Murray 1926, Chen 2012 and Franco 2015 in their docstrings; the math-KG YAML registers equations 1-5 with single-range code loci. Deductions: the Hill templates in `evaluate_notch_gain_sweep` (L1337-1349) and the regime branches at L313-380 are not documented as prescriptions in the module docstring, which still describes the sweep as reproducing the benchmark (-5); the lumenization coefficients and AV gains are uncited (-3); Panel E legend still reads \"Simulated (Pass 2)\" (L1831) and the lumen docstring (L680-681) is wrong about DAPT (-2); the counter-current comment at L761-765 claims a position-independence that the WT result contradicts (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py L1828–L1832: Panel E legend still says 'Simulated (Pass 2)'; refs_primary hard-coded here rather than read from the reference JSON <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py#L1828-L1832>",
        "2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py L761–L765: Comment claims counter-current layout makes competition calibre- rather than position-dependent; WT survivors cluster near the inlet with one 9 um rung <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py#L761-L765>" ;
