        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-model-fidelity-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-model-fidelity-6> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bentley, Gerhardt & Bates (2008) PLoS Comput. Biol., Hellström et al. (2007) Nature & Jakobsson et al. (2010) Nat. Cell Biol. VEGF-VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 tip/stalk salt-and-pepper lateral inhibition and angiogenic sprouting, coupled to lumenized Poiseuille flow, wall-shear pruning and arteriovenous specification (Pass 3) — Morphometric validation: 83/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L2045-2223) now returns 14 reference-anchored measurements; the five new hemodynamic metrics (L2078-2131) are WT median capillary wall shear stress 1.0555 Pa (ref 1.5, band 1-2), emergent Murray exponent 3.5264 (ref 3.0), max Kirchhoff residual 6.7e-26 m^3/s (ref 0), DAPT/WT perfused-density ratio 1.625 (ref 1.5, band 1.3-2.0) and WT AV segregation index 1.0 (ref 1.0; DAPT 0.5, no-flow 0.5), all with units, method, source and reference pulled from the SHA-256-pinned JSON; the nine Pass 2 values are unchanged. Deductions: measurement 7 (sweep Pearson r = 0.998, L2192-2201) is a template fit, not a simulation-vs-benchmark statistic (-5); measurements 8-9 (L2202-2221) use reference values 0.1967 and 0.8406 that are the script's own segmentation outputs, so they are self-referential (-4); measurements 1-6 compare regimes whose outcomes are steered by hard-coded branches (L313-380) to the benchmarks they were steered to (-3); the Murray exponent misses the band [2.7, 3.3] by 0.23 and the self-test widens the band by +/-0.4 to pass (L2307-2308) (-2); the AV index is saturated so measurement 14 hitting 1.0 is weakly discriminating, and three references are bands/qualitative rather than points (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py L2192–L2201: Measurement 7: Pearson r of the Section 4 sweep, whose k_t > 0 points are templates (circular) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py#L2192-L2201>",
        "2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py L2202–L2221: Measurements 8-9: reference_value 0.1967 / 0.8406 are the script's own specimen segmentation outputs, not external values <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py#L2202-L2221>",
        "2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py L2306–L2309: Self-test widens the Murray band by +/-0.4 (k = 3.53 vs band [2.7, 3.3]) to pass <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py#L2306-L2309>" ;
